# CODEOWNERS for webflow/ctxcop
#
# Branch protection requires CODEOWNER review on PRs touching security-
# sensitive paths. Catch-all is the maintainer pair; security-sensitive
# globs additionally require @webflow/infrastructure-security review so
# that detection logic, supply-chain config, and threat-model docs can't
# land on a single individual's approval.

# Catch-all
*                          @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security

# Workflow + supply-chain config — third-party deps and CI gates land here.
.github/workflows/*        @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
.github/ACTION_PIN_POLICY.md  @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
.github/action-allowlist.txt  @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
.goreleaser.yml            @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
go.mod                     @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
go.sum                     @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security

# Security-policy and threat-model docs.
SECURITY.md                @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
THREATMODEL.md             @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
THIRD_PARTY_AUDIT.md       @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security

# Detection layer — false negatives leak credentials.
internal/redact/**         @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
internal/rules/**          @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
internal/skiplist/**       @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security

# Harness adapters — wrong JSON shape is a silent leak.
internal/harness/**        @arr-wf @webflow/infrastructure-security
